nspawnmgr (0.7.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Changing a container user's password now also updates that user's
    stored RDP credential, so RDP sessions no longer fail with a stale
    password afterwards.
  * Remote-desktop (Guacamole) sessions now load correctly when nspawnmgr
    is reached through a reverse proxy: the session URL honors the
    forwarded protocol and host instead of producing a mixed-content
    (blank) frame.

 -- nspawnmgr packaging <packaging@nspawnmgr.invalid>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +1000

nspawnmgr (0.6.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * nspawnmgr can now be reached correctly through more than one public
    hostname at once - for example directly and through a reverse proxy in
    front of it - via a new "Additional trusted origins" setting under
    Auth on /admin/settings, without disturbing the existing Login URL.
  * Shared users can now start, stop, restart, pause, resume, and
    force-stop a container shared with them (previously limited to using
    its Scripts/SSH) - Delete remains owner-only.
  * A host reboot no longer strands managed containers on a self-assigned
    link-local address: the nspawnbr0/dnsmasq boot race is now
    self-healing, and container state left stale by a reboot (shown
    RUNNING when it no longer is) is automatically reconciled on startup
    and via a new "Reconcile machine states" button.
  * New "Enable enhanced networking" container option (grants CAP_NET_ADMIN
    and access to /dev/net/tun) lets a container run its own VPN/tunnel
    client.
  * Container package installs (DNF/APT/Pacman) now resolve dependencies
    from the local cache first, so they keep working even without live
    internet access once the needed packages are already cached.
  * New network diagnostics: a missing ufw DNS (port 53) rule on
    nspawnbr0, and outbound container traffic blocked by ufw.
  * The self-hosted nspawnmgr machine's own port mapping is now a real,
    editable entry in the normal Port mappings section instead of being
    hidden.
  * Fixed "Log in again" after logging out not returning to nspawnmgr.

 -- nspawnmgr packaging <packaging@nspawnmgr.invalid>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +1000

nspawnmgr (0.5.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Wayland desktop support: new containers can run a Wayland session (None,
    Sway, or Wayfire) instead of X11, streamed over VNC via wayvnc - each
    gets a real compositor, panel/wallpaper where applicable, and working
    keyboard/mouse input. Available on Fedora and Arch templates; gated off
    Debian's bookworm templates, whose packaged wlroots is too old for the
    input protocol wayvnc needs. KDE/Xfce Wayland sessions, GNOME's native
    RDP, and Hyprland were each investigated and are not offered - all hit
    real, currently-open upstream blockers unrelated to nspawnmgr's own code.
  * guacd's vendored FreeRDP upgraded to 3.5.1 (guacamole-server 1.6.0) for
    a more current, better-maintained RDP client implementation.
  * New Keystroke Button Panel: an admin-curated list of key combinations
    (Ctrl+Alt+Delete being the canonical example) shown as on-screen buttons
    on a container or host's session page, for keys a browser can never
    deliver as a real keypress. Configurable per machine, including at
    creation time.
  * Host management consolidated: RDP security, description, and sharing for
    external Hosts now live on one Edit Host page instead of being split
    across several places.
  * RDP reliability fixes: a stale VNC-side desktop session (XFCE or KDE)
    left over from an earlier connection no longer blocks a fresh RDP
    session from starting; xrdp's own TLS setup no longer intermittently
    fails from a missing group membership.
  * Numerous smaller reliability fixes (container-user password-toggle
    icon placement, Machines-list card layout, and more). See the project's
    git history for the full list.

 -- nspawnmgr packaging <packaging@nspawnmgr.invalid>  Sun, 06 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +1000

nspawnmgr (0.4.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Multilingual UI: the entire interface (every template, JS-built message,
    server-side validation/error message, and the Guacamole/database
    settings form) is now available in English, Spanish, French,
    Portuguese, Japanese, and Simplified Chinese, auto-detected from the
    browser's Accept-Language header with a per-user override on the
    Profile page. The administrator's guide is translated into all five
    non-English languages too. Protocol/technology names (SSH, RDP, VNC,
    NSPAWN, PODMAN, QEMU, and similar) are deliberately left untranslated
    throughout, as universal technical terms.
  * New host packaging: RPM (Fedora/RHEL, via dnf/rpmbuild), a plain Arch
    Linux package, and a SteamOS-specific variant (relocates all storage
    under /home for the Deck's small root partition, works around SteamOS's
    default firewalld/Gaming Mode quirks) - alongside the existing .deb.
  * Files browsing now works for QEMU VMs and any SSH-enabled Host, not just
    managed nspawn/podman containers - goes over SFTP against the target's
    own SSH server, with a per-session credential prompt (never stored) and
    the connected username shown next to Disconnect.
  * Package upgrades (upgrade-nspawnmgr.sh / a package manager's own
    upgrade) now fully reconcile the self-hosted machine's contents (JRE,
    WARs, guacd, systemd units, SSH credentials) on every run, not just a
    narrow WAR refresh - closing a real gap where a release needing a
    host-side change had no upgrade path short of a full reinstall.
  * Numerous smaller reliability fixes (package-download false-failures,
    dnsmasq/DHCP races on Arch-family installs, host-address/loopback
    diagnostics accuracy, and more). See the project's git history for the
    full list.

 -- nspawnmgr packaging <packaging@nspawnmgr.invalid>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +1000

nspawnmgr (0.3.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Podman and QEMU join systemd-nspawn as full container/VM backends: pods
    (podman, sharing the same nspawnbr0 bridge via netavark host-local IPAM)
    and QEMU/KVM virtual machines (configurable CPU/memory/NIC/pointer
    device, ISO boot media, disk cloning from a template), both alongside
    nspawn containers on one unified Machines page.
  * Redesigned UI: a persistent sidebar/topbar shell, a card-based Machines
    grid with backend badges and inline SSH/RDP/VNC/Files pills, and a
    Profile page with working logout.
  * Machine ownership and sharing are now enforced uniformly across every
    kind (nspawn, podman, QEMU, and admin-managed Hosts) - nothing is
    visible by default except to its owner, an admin, or someone it's been
    explicitly shared with; admins can take ownership of anything.
  * A Host's RUNNING/STOPPED state is now resolved live via a cached TCP
    reachability check instead of always showing RUNNING.
  * Numerous smaller reliability fixes. See the project's git history for
    the full list.

 -- nspawnmgr packaging <packaging@nspawnmgr.invalid>  Tue, 25 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +1000

nspawnmgr (0.2.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Substantial accumulation of fixes and features since the initial 0.1.0
    packaging, including: per-container RDP/VNC provisioning fixes across
    Fedora, Arch, and Debian; an optional PAM-based local-login bypass
    (pam_nspawnmgr) for containers whose own /etc/shadow auth is broken; a
    self-hosted deployment mode (nspawnmgr manages its own Tomcat/guacd
    inside a container it owns); refined container sharing/ownership and
    container-user management, including choosing which account SSH/RDP/VNC
    connect as; and numerous smaller reliability fixes. See the project's
    git history for the full list.

